<!--
  Dev-server fallback. The deployed copy is GENERATED by
  scripts/prerender-seo.mjs from `SITE.url` and the same route list that gets a
  prerendered head, so the live sitemap can never name a different origin than
  the canonicals do.

  Only pages a stranger should be able to land on. The booking wizard and the
  account area are excluded on purpose (see robots.txt) — a sitemap entry is a
  request to index, and asking for a sign-in wall to be indexed is asking for a
  thin page in the results.

  `priority` is relative within this file and `changefreq` is a hint; both are
  advisory. `lastmod` is the one search engines actually act on, so it is only
  worth keeping if it is kept honest — update the date on a page when its copy
  changes, not on every deploy.
-->
